{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And what proceeds from your mouth you shall do.</b> The intention in this statement is that they should not understand that he decreed for them the matter of building the cities etc. unconditionally; rather, it is a condition. Or it may intend to respond to what they said — that if they build fortified cities and settle their children there, they would be delayed until Israel takes possession of their inheritance in the land. Therefore he said <b>and what proceeds</b> etc. — meaning, this detail, had you not said it yourselves, there would be no need to be concerned that there is an issue; for your staying there until the completion of the seven years of conquest would have sufficed, and there would be no need to stay there fourteen years. But since you said this — what proceeds from your mouth you shall do. And you will find that Moses stipulated with them only until the land was conquered and not until it was divided, as stated in the language of the condition — to say that this condition is binding only to fulfill what proceeded from their mouth."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:16:47.021673536Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}